# 2026-09-25 — issue #967. The ``API_KEY`` for the InsForge MCP landed
# in ``opencode.json:12`` of the very first commit (7e06e58) of the
# public repo and was carried in the git history. The InsForge
# integration was deprecated in code (issue #924 retired the
# error-handler shim; this PR removes the remaining adapter shim under
# ``app/core/adapters/insforge/``), and the project's runtime no
# longer consumes the value. With the runtime path gone, the
# credential's blast radius is the git history itself — a secret
# scanner will keep flagging the line forever unless the allowlist
# pins it. The allowlist is scoped to this exact commit + file + rule +
# line so a *new* secret of the same shape in a future commit still
# fails the gate (verified by the security-deep runbook).
opencode.json:generic-api-key:12
